cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use vibe-sentinel in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: vibe-sentinel
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-09-03"
abstract: >
  Guards structural expectations about how a codebase is organized, and
  reports drift. Probes measure the shape of a tree — modules per package,
  commentary against code, where a pattern occurs, dependency licences and
  provenance, credentials at rest — and every run is recorded to an
  append-only history that later runs compare against. Three gates turn a
  measurement into a decision that must be pinned rather than suppressed.
  An optional PreToolUse hook journals a coding agent's commands and, when
  asked, reviews a dangerous one against what that agent already ran. Runs
  entirely on the user's machine via a local OpenAI-compatible model, and
  works without a model at all.
authors:
  - family-names: Samsonau
    given-names: Sergey V.
